{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each copy of a parallel edge gives a different path. A path reaching one target continues to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the others, so a path through a target to another is listed after the shorter one. The source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"itself, when it is a target, gives the trivial path first.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence holds the graph (a value), so iterating again gives the same paths. The first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the rows the source reaches, O(n + m). A vertex that reaches no target is never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entered, but a partial path can still end where every way on is blocked by its own vertices,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the time between two paths is not bounded by a polynomial in n + m."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/directedsimplepaths"]}],"metadata":{"title":"DirectedSimplePaths","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/SimplePaths.swift#L222","fileName":"SimplePaths.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}],"externalID":"s:9Traversal19DirectedSimplePathsV"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Every simple path of a directed graph from a source to any of a set of targets, lazily, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order a depth-first search from the source, taking out-edges in ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, reaches them.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Iterator"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/maxLength"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/makeIterator()"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Element"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Sequence-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Defa